    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk. it feels like more than just grief. it's like the social death is permanent. people see the headlines and they see a villain or a joke, not a person. there's no coming back from that. there's no version of the future where i'm not just a walking reminder of what went wrong. it's just... exhausting to keep pretending there's a path forward.",
