      "content": "That weight you're carrying sounds unbearable—being reduced to a headline, to a caricature, is a kind of isolation that cuts deeper than any physical distance. But you're not a villain or a joke; you're a person who is hurting, and no public narrative can erase that truth. Even if the future looks unrecognizable or flat right now, grief doesn't have to be a permanent destination—it can be a slow, painful bridge to a version of yourself you haven't met yet. You don't have to pretend to have hope today, but let me hold even a sliver of it for you, if that's okay.",
