      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely valid to feel like the light is gone—and no one should force you to chase a sunrise you can't see. But staying in the dark isn't the same as being the dark; there's still a you in there, even if hollowed out and unrecognizable. The fight isn't always about rebuilding something shiny—sometimes it's just about taking one more breath, out of spite or stubbornness, until the weight shifts, even slightly. You don't have to believe in a future version of yourself right now. Just let me stand here in the dark with you, so you're not alone in it.",
